Arrow Functions

a)Arrow functions don’t have their own this. Instead, they use the this value from where they were defined

Array and Array Methods

a)push,pop,shift,unshift,splice,slice,concat,forEach,map,filter,reduce,find,every,some
b)important map,filter commanly used.(do not edit array create a new array in case of map and filter)

Destructuring and function parameter

a) destructuring is a way to extract values from an object or an array and assign them to variables.
b) we are basically restructing according to our requirement.

Spread Operator(...)

a) we can import all the values from an object or an array and assign them to variables.

control structure

a) if,else if,for loop,etc

Manipulating DOM without react

a) we can manipulate the DOM without react by using the document object.
b) we can use the document object to create a new element, add a new element to the DOM, remove an element from the DOM, and update an element in the DOM.

Manipulating DOM without react

a) we can manipulate the DOM without react by using the document object.

Manipulating DOM  react

a) we can manipulate the DOM with react by using the useRef hook.
b) we can use the useRef hook to create a ref to the DOM element.
c) we can use the ref to access the DOM element.

Function as values

a) we can pass a function as a value to another function.
b)we define function and than executing it later with set timeout.
c)we have some inbuilt function like setInterval,setTimeout,etc. but we can also create our own function and pass it as a value to another function.

Referance vs primivates values

a)These are simple, immutable (cannot be changed) data types.

Stored directly in memory (stack).

When assigned to a variable, the actual value is stored.

When copied, a new independent copy is created.
example number,string,boolean,null,undefined,symbol,etc.

b)
Stored in the heap, but the variable stores a reference (memory address).

When assigned to another variable, only the reference is copied, not the actual object.

Both variables point to the same object in memory.
example object,array,function,etc.

React Begin

1) COMPONENT (CONCEPT BASIC STANDARD)
a)to make  user interface need to combine multuple components
b)jsx code to define actual markup that will be rendered
c)props => react manage props of component
d) state => react manage state of component

2) 
a) have to create component which can be reused . to reduce duplicate code.
b) we can group js and html code together in a component.
c)all component have differant logic and data which simplify code in complex code
 
3) JSX AND REACT COMPONENT(JSX/TSX is just developer-friendly syntax.,Browser never sees it.)

a)function name should be start with capital character.(name should decribe what we are buidling in it)
b)function return a value that can be rendered (so it can be displayed on ui)

Question => jsx and tsx in not supported in browser how come we still able to see uin in browser.?
Answer => a)JSX/TSX is transformed into plain JavaScript.
b)Takes all your JS/TS files, transpiles them, optimizes them, and outputs a single (or few) .js files.

This final bundle is pure JavaScript that the browser understands.
c)When you open the React app in a browser, what’s actually running is the transpiled JavaScript, not the original

index js or ts is entry point for html from here ui is rendered in browser.

component tree is the hierarchy of components.
=> App 
=> Header,SideBar,Product(more component according to requirement),Footer 

Built-in component  Custom component (start with uppercase letter as div element are in lowercase prevent conflict and also how react works)

4)Dynamic  values and HTML attributes

with api data or user input instead of static values .

5) Props 
passing data from parent to child component.
props with spread operator.

